# Honeypot runtime data, never committed.
#
# The directory skeleton below is tracked on purpose. compose.yaml bind mounts
# this directory over the Cowrie image's own /cowrie/cowrie-git/var, which
# replaces the tree the image ships with, and Cowrie does not create the log
# directory it writes to. Without the skeleton in version control a fresh clone
# would fail to start with "No such file or directory: var/log/cowrie/cowrie.json".
#
# This directory corresponds to the *inside* of that mount point, so `log/`
# here is `var/log/` in the container and `lib/` is `var/lib/`.
#
# Each directory carries its own .gitignore, the same convention the Cowrie image
# uses, so the layout is preserved while the generated files stay out of git.
# The negations below hand the tree over to those nested files, which then ignore
# whatever each directory actually generates.
*
!.gitignore
!log
!log/**
!lib
!lib/**
!run
!run/**
